{
  "x-call": "wingtip_airspace::sua_tab::call",
  "description": "The tab ForeFlight writes on a special-use area's boundary, its words: the area's name cut to nine characters after the type's letter (\"M-BRADY NOR*\"), and its floor and ceiling as figures with their references (SFC, AGL, MSL, FL, UNL), from the FAA's special use airspace data (ADDS: each limit's VAL in feet, a flight level times 100, its CODE SFC, MSL, STD or UNLTD and its DESC TI, TNI or ANI). Written as the FAA's CIFP writes the same areas: a ceiling \"to but not including\" FL180 is 17,999 ft MSL, as Class A begins at 18,000 ft MSL (14 CFR 71.33); another ceiling TNI a foot under its figure, a floor ANI a foot over it; SFC above 0 is that height AGL. Null for a piece the FAA cuts out of its area (EXCLUSION 1), or where a limit has no figure.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "input": {
      "title": "SpecialUseTabInput",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
